Z||000003||mrfiero||08-26-2000||01:15 AM||||Check the fuses first.  Each bank of cylinders has its own fuse....one of yours may have blown.  This is the easiest one to check, so do it first!   ||||reg||3
Z||000004||WisconsinGT||08-26-2000||04:26 AM||||MrFiero, can you tell me where/how to check the fuses for the cylinders? I have always wanted to check them, but not sure how. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||08-26-2000||06:10 AM||||Look at the fuse box in the drivers side footwell.  There will be 2 fuses, one for the left bank injectors and one for the right.  They will be labeled "TBI INJ 1" and "TBI INJ 2", right behind the fuel pump fuse.  <P>If it does sound like only 1 bank of pistons is firing, then it definatly has something to do with injector wiring.  <P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 149,000 miles and counting!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">   <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FieroGTRacingInc||08-26-2000||09:05 AM||||yep....   my inj 2 fuse was blown......  it keep blowing fuses though... even a 25....<P>where do I start looking for the reason for blowing them???  thank's..||||reg||1
Z||000007||ourufo||08-26-2000||01:04 PM||||Please dont ever put in a larger fuse then required.  <BR>wire in a low amp circut breaker,with a spaid end to plug into the fuse slot then set a test lightfrom the other end of the breaker to the other spaid of the fuse box.<BR>when the breaker opens the test light goes out. during the time  the lite is on you can shakes wires and check for shorts.<BR><P>------------------<BR>OURUFOV8||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||08-26-2000||09:42 PM||||Disconnect C520, the connector on the engine to the injectors. This will isolate the injectors and the wiring.<P>TBI INJ 2 also supplies the EGR solenoid. Disconnect that too.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 08-26-2000).]||||reg||1
