Z||000024||Oreif||08-31-2000||09:46 AM||||OK, Sounds like the problem is not with the timing chain. Here's some things to try. First are you sure the spark is strong enough? Had a car where it appeared we got spark but it wasn't strong enough. The spark should jump 1/2" of air gap with a loud snap. If catalytic converter is clogged you will have too much backpressure and the car won't run. Since you smell gas, I would pull all the spark plugs and see if they are wet. If they are, leave them out to dry out the excess fuel. This gives you a chance to examine the plugs.<BR>You could also check the ignition module in the distributor. These have caused simular problems too and can die suddenly due to heat fatigue.<BR>I reread your initial post, I would check cat for clogging and the ignition module first. From what you say above you had a loss of power then it died. This is a common symptom of them. <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000025||Indiana_resto_guy||08-31-2000||10:21 PM||||When you try to start is it turning over normally or turning really really fast?<BR>I just pulled the distriubtor ot of mine for a change out and it was a real ba%$#rd to get it to the correct spot again, but I have a slim balancer on with three marks on it. If you think that your at TDC for #1 and still doesn't start but back fires, Pull it (the distriubtor) out and turn it 180* and try again.||||reg||1
Z||000026||1FieroGTRacingInc||08-31-2000||11:41 PM||||Orief....<BR>  I have a straight pipe w/ no cat.... and my plug's are dry ...  i am getting good spark for sure...<P>Indiana.... it is just turning over  just normal<P>something just hit me like a Pontiac...lol<P>I originally thought that i had a timing problem right...<BR>so i adjusted the distr. to try to set the timing when someone mentioned  disconnecting my battery to reset the ECM, so i did....  NOW IS WHEN IT WON'T START... DID I LOSE SOMETHING .. WHEN MY TIMING WAS SCREWED UP WHEN I RESET MY ECM???   that's why   Right??<P>I had blown my TBI INJ#2 fuse when my EGR plug fell into the belt's going down the road...  hhmmm.... <P>am I crazy??||||reg||1
Z||000027||Indiana_resto_guy||09-01-2000||10:04 AM||||Re-check your fuses, injectors, crank, ecm, fuel pump (fuse & relay)<BR>When you turn key to 'ON' (not starting) does the chck engine lite come on and do you hear the fuel pump for 2-3 seconds? This will take care of the fuel pump relay and fuse if you hear it run and the ECM fuse if lite comes on.<BR>Re-check your wiring repairs (I hope you used butt connectors or something similar instead of just 'twisting them together').<BR>When you went to TDC, how did you determine that you were on the compression stroke of #1? If your plugs are dry after several attempts at starting your not getting fuel to the injectors.<BR>When you set your timing since you don't have a light, keep computer in it's normal mode and set your timing by idle when 'warm' (normal operating temp) to 1K to 1.1K R.P.M.'s.||||reg||1
